{
  "id": "behavioral-criterion",
  "term": "behavioral criterion",
  "definition": "A behavioral criterion is an observable performance standard used to judge whether a person is ready for a target behavior or intervention. In this context, it refers to using pill-taking practice performance to decide adherence readiness and when treatment should begin.",
